# {{ module_path }}

Generated Go SDK package.

Operations accept `(ctx, *OperationParams, ...RequestOption)`. Supply required
fields in a struct literal and optional values with fluent `WithX(value)` setters.
`WithoutX()` clears optional fields. Setters mutate and return their receiver.
Nullable model fields also provide `WithXNull()` for explicit JSON null.

Required fields are plain Go values, including their zero values. Passing nil
params is allowed only when the operation has no required inputs. Optional whole
JSON bodies distinguish omission from an explicitly supplied nil payload.
Model collection fields retain their generated `omitempty` behavior.

Transport settings are supplied with `WithRequestOptions(RequestOptions{...})`.
Options run once per call in order; the last `WithRequestOptions` replaces previous
per-call settings. Raw methods return the HTTP response without decoding it.

This calling convention replaces positional operation inputs from SDKs generated
by Arvalez 1. See `params.go` for operation input types and `models.go` for bodies.
